.TH READRSS 1 "" "readrss" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
readrss \- desktop RSS/Atom feed reader
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B readrss
.RB [ \-\-background ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B readrss
is a GTK4/libadwaita feed reader. It shows the feed summary, extracts the full article or
opens the original page inside the app, filters articles per feed by keywords or regular
expressions and syncs in the background with desktop notifications.
.PP
Only one instance runs per user session: starting
.B readrss
again shows the window of the running instance.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-background
Start without opening the window, syncing and notifying in the background. Used by the
systemd user service.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show the available options.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/readrss/readrss.db
Feeds, articles, filters and preferences (SQLite).
.TP
.I ~/.cache/readrss/icons/
Cached website icons.
.TP
.I /usr/lib/systemd/user/readrss.service
User service that starts with the graphical session. Disable it for your user with
.BR "systemctl \-\-user mask readrss" .
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR systemctl (1)
.PP
https://github.com/EmersonComar/readrss
